# PortSwigger Web Security Academy

## Server-side prototype pollution via error handling

### Objective

The objective of this lab was to identify and exploit a **server-side prototype pollution vulnerability** in the `/my-account/change-address` endpoint.

The application accepts user-controlled JSON data and processes it server-side. By manipulating the special `__proto__` property, it was possible to inject arbitrary properties into the server-side JavaScript object prototype.

The vulnerability was confirmed by first injecting an arbitrary `foo` property and subsequently abusing the application's error-handling mechanism to modify the `status` and `statusCode` values returned in JSON error responses.

The final exploitation chain was:

```text
Attacker-controlled JSON
        ↓
__proto__
        ↓
Object.prototype pollution
        ↓
status = 555
        ↓
Error object inherits polluted property
        ↓
statusCode = 555
        ↓
Prototype pollution confirmed
```

